- windows desktop freezing high cpu memory
- windows update error computer performance
- windows 11 crashes blue screen system
- computer running slow storage drive nearly full','305defcffe993a135953f9879cb1e7865b03a7aae4c872d48f3089fa4d022d2b');
INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks(chunk_id,document_id,ordinal,heading,content,content_hash) VALUES('kb-endpoint-windows-performance--02-working-hypothesis','kb-endpoint-windows-performance','2','Working hypothesis','Low disk space, a recent change or resource pressure may be causing Windows performance issues.','9c4b55cd1809f42fdbf39c02e0ff32ba743e03cb9ff580e4d6b32a58e22f54e1');
INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks(chunk_id,document_id,ordinal,heading,content,content_hash) VALUES('kb-endpoint-windows-performance--03-troubleshooting','kb-endpoint-windows-performance','3','Troubleshooting','1. Capture symptoms, start time and recent software or Windows updates.
2. Check free disk space, Task Manager and relevant Event Viewer entries.
3. Compare the impact before and after the recent change; preserve diagnostic evidence.
4. Use approved cleanup options after checking user data and backup status.
5. Validate performance with the user; escalate repeat crashes or suspected hardware faults.','19b899475218b67c5161b72719312eb51a27d8018ab7f184a82d53abed4e1357');
